cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MIRA in your research, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "MIRA: Bayesian Multilevel Inference for Longitudinal Data"
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-10-03"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23120184"
authors:
  - family-names: Celani
    given-names: Davide
    email: davide.celani.00@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/davide-celani/MIRA"
url: "https://github.com/davide-celani/MIRA"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  MIRA is an R package for Bayesian multilevel modeling of continuous
  longitudinal outcomes using Stan. It supports Student-t, Gaussian,
  and log-normal observation models, multiple treatment arms, subject-level
  covariates, configurable priors, and posterior probabilities of meaningful
  change. The package also provides longitudinal data exploration,
  frequentist analyses, and reproducible report generation.
keywords:
  - R
  - Stan
  - Bayesian inference
  - multilevel modeling
  - longitudinal data
  - repeated measures
  - clinical research
